1. Explain the difference between Frontend, Backend, and Full-Stack Development with suitable real-world examples.
Ans- 
Frontend Development:
It is the visible part of a website that users can see and interact with.
It is developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
It focuses on the design and user experience.
Example: The homepage of Amazon or the Instagram login page.

Backend Development:
It is the server-side part of a website.
It processes requests, manages data, and communicates with the database.
It is developed using languages like Java, Python, PHP, or Node.js.
Example: Verifying login details or processing online payments.

Full-Stack Development:
A Full-Stack Developer works on both the frontend and backend.
They build the complete website from user interface to database.
Example: Developing an entire e-commerce website like Amazon.


3. Describe how a browser requests and displays a web page from a web server.
Ans-
The user enters a website URL in the browser.
The browser sends a request to the web server.
The web server processes the request.
The server sends the required files (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, images) back to the browser.
The browser reads these files and displays the web page to the user.


