5. Explain what a web server is and give examples of commonly used servers.

Ans-
A web server is a computer or software that stores website files and sends them to users when they request a web page through a browser.

Examples of Web Servers:

Apache HTTP Server
Nginx
Microsoft IIS
LiteSpeed
Node.js (Express)


6. Define the roles of a Frontend Developer, Backend Developer, and Database Administrator in a project.
Ans-
Frontend Developer:
Designs the user interface.
Creates web pages using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
Makes the website responsive and user-friendly.

Backend Developer:
Develops server-side logic.
Connects the website with the database.
Handles login, authentication, and data processing.

Database Administrator (DBA):
Manages and maintains databases.
Stores, secures, and backs up data.
Ensures data is available and organized.

