8. Explain the difference between static and dynamic websites. Provide an example of each.
Ans: 
Static Website:
Shows the same content to every user.
Does not use a database.
Simple and fast.
Example: Personal portfolio website.

Dynamic Website:
Content changes based on the user or data.
Uses a database.
More interactive.
Example: Amazon, Facebook, Instagram.


9. Research and list five web browsers. Explain how rendering engines differ between them.
Ans-
Five Web Browsers:
Google Chrome
Mozilla Firefox
Microsoft Edge
Apple Safari
Opera

Rendering Engines:
Google Chrome: Blink
Microsoft Edge: Blink
Mozilla Firefox: Gecko
Apple Safari: WebKit
Opera: Blink

Difference

A rendering engine converts HTML, CSS, and JavaScript into the web page that users see. Different browsers use different rendering engines, so websites may look or perform slightly differently on each browser.